course: dictionary
lesson: 12244
title: Secret plans and bad luck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To conspire means to plan something secretly with other people, usually something bad or against the law. The context clues are the secret and the bad aim. «The guards conspired to free the prisoner in the night.» The word night and the idea of freeing a prisoner tell you it was a secret plan.
explain: Sometimes things conspire without any people planning at all. «Everything conspired to make us late.» The rain, the traffic and the flat tyre all went wrong together, so it felt as if they were plotting against us. Ask yourself: is someone secretly planning this, or is bad luck piling up?
explain: Conspire can also be playful. «The twins conspired to hide a birthday cake in the shed.» Nobody is doing anything wicked. Two people are working together in secret to make a surprise, so the word means a friendly secret plan.
fact: Conspire is a verb: conspire, conspires, conspired, conspiring.
fact: «Conspire» means to plan together in secret, often to do something bad or against the law.
fact: When events conspire, several things happen together and cause a bad result, as if they were planned.
fact: Playful «conspire» can mean planning a secret surprise, such as «conspired to throw a party».
fact: Useful phrases: «conspire against» (plan against someone), «conspire to do» (plan to do something), «conspire with» (plan together with someone).
exercise: «The guards conspired to free the prisoner in the night.» What does conspired mean? | Shouted loudly for help | *Secretly planned together | Ate a big dinner | Went to sleep early
exercise: «Everything conspired to make us late.» What does conspired suggest? | We planned the trip together with a map | The bus was early and we arrived first | The match started on time | *Several bad things happened together and caused a bad result
exercise: «The twins conspired to hide a birthday cake in the shed.» What does conspire mean here? | Broke the cake into pieces | Forgot where the shed was | *Planned together in secret | Argued loudly about the cake
test: «The king's advisers conspired against him, hoping to take his throne.» Find and copy the word that means plotted in secret. | king's | advisers | *conspired | throne
test: Which word is closest in meaning to conspire when it means a secret plan? | sleep | wander | *plot | smile
exam: Which sentence uses conspire in the playful way? | The thieves conspired to break into the bank at midnight. | Everything conspired against the team on the wet, muddy day. | *The sisters conspired to plan a surprise picnic for Mum. | The soldiers conspired to overthrow the old king.
